    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created (and read back), the response now includes `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** I touched 2 files and modified exactly one function (`toOwnerDto`, cyclomatic complexity 1) by adding a single annotation line, rather than growing any method or class. The schema field is generated code (no hand-written function), and no new branching or method bodies were introduced. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
